# Standard icon pack (`IOS_ICONS`)

The project's shared icon set lives in **`public/admin/admin-ui.js`** as `IOS_ICONS` (Lucide-style stroke SVGs, `currentColor`). Helpers: `iosIcon(key, size)`, `createIosIconBtn({ size })`, `createAgentBtn`, `agentIconSvg`.

Icon-only buttons take `size: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg'`. That class locks the hit box and glyph (`24/12`, `36/16`, `44/20`). Default is `md` — the same box as the circular agent control. Do not override width/height in a one-off stylesheet; pick a size.

## Always reuse — never invent

Before adding any icon (toolbar button, header control, panel action, empty state, search clear, sheet close, etc.):

1. Check whether the key already exists on `IOS_ICONS`.
2. If it does, use that SVG — via `iosIcon('x', 16)` / `IOS_ICONS.x` / `createIosIconBtn({ iconKey })` in admin client JS.
3. If it does not, **add the icon to `IOS_ICONS` first**, then consume it. Do not paste a one-off SVG elsewhere and leave the pack incomplete.
4. Do not freestyle filled / alternate shapes when a pack glyph exists or belongs in the pack. Match the existing stroke style (`fill="none"`, `stroke="currentColor"`, `stroke-width="1.75"` unless neighbors differ).
5. Need a different pixel size? Call `iosIcon(key, size)` — never duplicate the path just to change width/height.

## Astro / SSR / React markup

These cannot import the admin client module. When an icon must appear in Astro or React:

- Copy the **exact** path data from `IOS_ICONS.<key>` (width/height may differ).
- Leave an HTML/JSX comment pointing at the pack key (e.g. `<!-- IOS_ICONS.bell — keep in sync with public/admin/admin-ui.js -->`).
- If you change the pack glyph, update every inlined copy in the same change.

## Do not

- Hand-draw or AI-generate a new bell / trash / share / x / search / etc. when the pack already has one (or should get one).
- Introduce a second icon library (Heroicons, Phosphor, Material, emoji-as-UI) for chrome that `IOS_ICONS` covers.
- Use filled solid variants that break visual consistency with the stroke set.
- Keep a private `const FOO_ICON = '<svg…>'` next to code that already imports `admin-ui.js` — use the pack.
- **Never invent brand / payment / product marks** (Apple Pay, Venmo, Visa, Cal.com, etc.). Use the **`simple-icons`** package (or `SIMPLE_ICONS_CDN` / existing `/stack/*` assets). For generic money UI (cash, credit card), use **`lucide-astro`** (`Banknote`, `CreditCard`, …) — not freestyled SVGs.

Brand logos come from Simple Icons (or company-supplied files). Photographic assets are separate. OS map node path tables in `os-map-loader.js` are map-specific and out of scope for the toolbar pack.
